==Sanskrit==

===Adjective===
{{head|sa|adjective|tr=bhā́rata}}

# descended from {{m|sa|भरत|tr=bharata}} or the [[Bhāratas]] (applied to [[Agni]] either "sprung from the priests called Bharatas" or "bearer of the [[oblation]]")
# belonging or relating to the Bharatas
## (with {{m|sa|युद्ध|tr=yuddha}}, {{m|sa|संग्राम|tr=saṃgrāma}}, {{m|sa|समर|tr=samara}}, {{m|sa|समिति|tr=samiti}}) the war or battle of the bharatas
## (with or scil. {{m|sa|आख्यान|tr=ākhyāna}} with {{m|sa|इतिहास|tr=itihāsa}} and {{m|sa|कथा|tr=kathā}}) the story of the Bharatas, the history or narrative of their war
## (with or scil. {{m|sa|मण्डल|tr=maṇḍala}} or {{m|sa|वर्ष|tr=varṣa}}) "king Bharatas's realm" i.e. [[India]]
# inhabiting {{m|sa|भरतवर्ष|tr=bharata-varṣa}} i.e. [[India]]; [[Indic]]

====Declension====
{{sa-decl-adj|भार|त|bhāra|t|a|ī|a}}

===Noun===
{{sa-noun|tr=bhā́rata|g=m}}

# a [[descendant]] of [[Bharata]] (also in pl. for [[Bharatās]])
# (with {{m|sa|अश्वमेध|tr=aśva-medha}}), name of the author of Rigveda V, 27
# (with {{m|as|देववात|tr=deva-vāta}} and {{m|sa|देवश्रवस्|tr=deva-śravas}}), name of the authors of Rigveda III, 23
# [[fire]]
# an [[actor]] (compare {{m|sa|भरत|tr=bharata}})
# name of the sun shining on the south of {{m|sa|मेरु|tr=meru}}

====Declension====
{{sa-decl-noun-a-m|भार|त|bhāra|t}}

===Noun===
{{sa-noun|tr=bhā́rata|g=n}}

# the [[land]] of Bharatas i.e. [[India]] (compare above)
# the story of the Bharatas and their wars (sometimes identified with the {{m|sa|महाभारत|tr=mahā-bhārata}}, and sometimes distinguished from it)
# (with {{m|sa|सरस्|tr=saras}}) name of a lake

====Declension====
{{sa-decl-noun-a-n|भार|त|bhāra|t}}

